<title>FRANCE: France slightly raises 1997 maize area estimate.</title>
<headline>France slightly raises 1997 maize area estimate.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's farm ministry said on Friday it slightly revised its estimate of the total area sown to maize in 1997 to 1.776 million hectares from 1.769 million last month.</p>
<p>That would represent a 2.7 percent rise over the 1.729 million hectares sown in 1996.</p>
<p>Sowings rose in the Alsace, Pays de Loire, Aquitaine, Midi-Pyrenees and Rhone-Alpes regions, but declined in Poitou Charentes.</p>
<p>Area was steady in Britanny and Center France.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
